# Responsive Design Guidelines

All UI components must look good and function well across all screen sizes.

## Core Principles

1. **Mobile-First Approach**
   - Design for mobile screens first
   - Enhance layout progressively for larger screens
   - Base styles (no prefix) should work for mobile

2. **Required Breakpoint Testing**
   - Mobile: < 640px (base styles)
   - Tablet: `sm:` (640px+)
   - Desktop: `md:` (768px+)
   - Large Desktop: `lg:` (1024px+)

## Tailwind Responsive Patterns

### Container Widths
```jsx
// Good: Responsive max-width
<Card className="w-full max-w-md md:max-w-lg lg:max-w-2xl">

// Bad: Fixed width
<Card className="w-[400px]">
```

### Typography Scaling
```jsx
// Good: Scale headings for desktop
<h2 className="text-2xl md:text-3xl lg:text-4xl">

// Good: Scale body text
<p className="text-sm md:text-base lg:text-lg">
```

### Padding and Spacing
```jsx
// Good: More breathing room on desktop
<CardContent className="p-4 sm:p-6 md:p-8 lg:p-10">

// Good: Responsive gaps
<div className="gap-3 md:gap-4 lg:gap-6">
```

### Layout Patterns
```jsx
// Good: Stack on mobile, side-by-side on desktop
<div className="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-3 md:gap-4">

// Good: Grid with responsive columns
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
```

### Buttons
```jsx
// Good: Full-width on mobile, flex on desktop
<Button className="w-full md:w-auto md:flex-1">

// Good: Stacked on mobile, row on desktop
<div className="flex flex-col gap-3 md:flex-row md:gap-4">
  <Button className="w-full md:flex-1">Primary</Button>
  <Button className="w-full md:flex-1">Secondary</Button>
</div>
```

### Show/Hide Content
```jsx
// Good: Show truncated on mobile, full on desktop
<span className="md:hidden">{id.slice(0, 12)}...</span>
<span className="hidden md:inline">{id}</span>
```

### Icon Sizes
```jsx
// Good: Scale icons with screen size
<Check className="h-10 w-10 md:h-12 md:w-12" />
```

## Checklist Before Shipping

- [ ] **Use Playwright to verify** - Take screenshots at different viewports
- [ ] Tested at mobile width (375px)
- [ ] Tested at tablet width (768px)
- [ ] Tested at desktop width (1024px+)
- [ ] Text is readable at all sizes
- [ ] Buttons are easily tappable on mobile (min 44px touch target)
- [ ] No horizontal scroll on any viewport
- [ ] No text overflow (use `truncate` with `max-w-*` for long text)
- [ ] Images scale appropriately
- [ ] Forms are usable on all devices

## Playwright Verification

Always verify UI designs with Playwright before considering them done:

```javascript
// Navigate to the page
browser_navigate({ url: "http://localhost:3000/page" })

// Test desktop view (1280px)
browser_resize({ width: 1280, height: 800 })
browser_take_screenshot({ type: "png", filename: "desktop.png" })

// Test mobile view (375px)
browser_resize({ width: 375, height: 812 })
browser_take_screenshot({ type: "png", filename: "mobile.png", fullPage: true })
```

## Desktop Layout Patterns

On desktop, prefer horizontal/landscape layouts over tall vertical cards:

```jsx
// Good: Two-column on desktop, stacked on mobile
<Card className="lg:max-w-4xl">
  <div className="lg:flex lg:gap-10">
    {/* Left column */}
    <div className="lg:w-1/3 lg:border-r lg:pr-10">
      {/* Success message, icon */}
    </div>
    {/* Right column */}
    <div className="mt-6 lg:mt-0 lg:flex-1">
      {/* Details, actions */}
    </div>
  </div>
</Card>
```

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

1. **Fixed pixel widths** - Use max-width with responsive values
2. **Tiny touch targets** - Ensure buttons are at least 44px on mobile
3. **Text too small on desktop** - Scale up for larger screens
4. **No breathing room** - Increase padding on larger screens
5. **Always stacked layouts** - Use horizontal layouts on desktop when space allows
6. **Portrait cards on desktop** - Cards should be landscape/horizontal on wide screens
7. **Text overflow** - Always use `truncate` or `break-words` for dynamic content
8. **Not verifying with Playwright** - Always take screenshots to verify the design
